85
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:52,760
Raw meat is made up of water, fat, and protein.

86
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:58,240
These protein molecules are wound up in coils and held together by bonds.

87
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:04,360
When meat is cooked, the heat breaks these bonds, causing the protein molecules to unwind,

88
00:06:04,361 --> 00:06:06,785
a process called denaturing.

89
00:06:06,786 --> 00:06:11,980
As the temperature rises, the proteins reconnect and shrink,

90
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:14,469
squeezing out water molecules.

91
00:06:14,470 --> 00:06:18,120
The hotter the meat's internal temperature, the more water

92
00:06:18,121 --> 00:06:24,421
gets pushed out. As the water evaporates, fat melts from the heat.

93
00:06:24,422 --> 00:06:26,140
Fat and water loss

94
00:06:26,141 --> 00:06:33,660
is why meat reduces in size when cooked. But meat reduction was nothing the supposed

95
00:06:33,661 --> 00:06:36,340
first hamburger eaters would have worried too much about,

96
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:39,900
since they ate their ground meat raw.

97
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:44,080
Genghis Khan and his army of Mongol horsemen

98
